consult a professional the  last thing that we want is our own sleep  deprivation and our own  lack of personal physical and mental  health to translate into an unsafe work  environment focusing on personal health  in order to care for others health jamie  morocco global news toronto  next the road to queen elizabeth's  unprecedented platinum jubilee  britain's longest reigning monarch has  the crown's future in mind she's  expressing support for prince charles's  wife camilla wishing her to become queen  consort once charles is king the  announcement comes as part of a  statement for the queen's platinum  jubilee it's been exactly 70 years since  elizabeth took the throne after her  father's death and as britain celebrates  the unprecedented milestone redmond  shannon looks at the long and bumpy road  leading up to it  you might say this is william roach  during queen elizabeth's 70th year on  the throne the world's longest reigning  monarch visited the world's longest  running soap opera the aptly named  coronation street one of tens of  thousands of engagements over her  remarkable reign seven decades that  began in east africa  it was on february 6 1952 that her  husband prince philip broke the news  during a visit to kenya her father king  george had died and she was now queen  it would be more than a year later  before the official coronation ceremony  when a struggling post-war britain was  transfixed by a young queen  a number of families went to  a neighbor's house the only neighbor in  the street who had a television  and we were all crammed into their  front room princess elizabeth was seen  symbolically to represent the  possibility of some public flowering of  a new elizabethan age royal commentator  richard fitzwilliams says the first  decades of her reign were relatively  smooth until the crisis of the 1990s you  had the so-called anas herbalists in  1992  that year saw the marriages of three of  her children fall apart under the public  gaze there was a major fire at windsor  castle and a tussle over whether the  royals should pay income tax  the absolute low point of her reign came  in 1997 when the british public angrily  demanded the queen return to london  after the death of princess diana  but from that moment on her popularity  rose and has stayed high since polls  suggest a strong support in britain for  the royal institution she exemplifies  duty and service to the country which is  why we in the army sort of love her so  much  through the highs of the royal weddings  of the 2010s to the recent lows of the  departure of prince harry from royal  duties as well as the ongoing  allegations of sexual assault against  her son prince andrew and of course the  death of her husband prince philip we've  seen the queen as an exemplar of what an  ideal monarch should be at the age of 95  and after a hospital stay last fall her  duties are being scaled back to match  her years but she is showing little  desire to retire from her life of duty  least of all during this record-breaking  jubilee year redmond shannon global news  london  and that is global national for this  sunday night i'm colleen christie  tonight your canada is calgary alberta  we love to see your corner of the  country so please keep sending your  photos to viewers at globalnational.com  thanks for watching donna friesen will  be back at the anchor desk tomorrow have  a great night  [Music]  you
 

